Backend Alembic Usage (Modular Only)

This Alembic setup is backend-only and must not depend on deprecated `app/` modules.

Paths
- Alembic config: `/app/backend/alembic.ini`
- Alembic scripts: `/app/backend/alembic`
- Revisions: `/app/backend/alembic/versions`

Required environment
- `DATABASE_URL` must be set (used by `backend/alembic/env.py` via `get_database_url()`).
- `POSTGRES_APP_SCHEMA` optional; defaults to `public`.

Run migrations
```bash
cd /app/backend
alembic -c /app/backend/alembic.ini upgrade head
```

Create a revision manually
```bash
cd /app/backend
alembic -c /app/backend/alembic.ini revision -m "your_change"
```

Create autogenerate revision
```bash
cd /app/backend
alembic -c /app/backend/alembic.ini revision --autogenerate -m "your_change"
```

Downgrade one step
```bash
cd /app/backend
alembic -c /app/backend/alembic.ini downgrade -1
```

Notes
- Keep Alembic revision IDs <= 32 chars because Alembic version table uses `VARCHAR(32)` by default.
- Startup bootstrap should run Alembic before seed/bootstrap admin.
- If Alembic config is missing, seed should be skipped safely to avoid schema-drift crashes.
